; =====================================================================
; basic-transport.abnf
;
; VERBATIM -- this is RFC 9804's own grammar, copied unchanged.
; It was NOT authored by this project. Do not edit it, do not correct
; it, do not reformat it. Defects found in it are recorded in
; README.md, never repaired here.
;
; Locator:  RFC 9804, "Simple Public Key Infrastructure (SPKI)
;           S-Expressions", Rivest & Eastlake, June 2025,
;           Informational, ISSN 2070-1721.
;           Section 7.3, "ABNF for Basic Transport".
;           Source text lines 783-787.
;           <https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9804.txt>
;
; Source digest (sha256 of the full source text):
;   0db36cc4bb9d0e08c4999ab775c955daec0f62e849bbfe688e223998d5a44434
;
; Verbatim region digest (sha256 of the bytes between the BEGIN and END
; markers below, markers excluded):
;   367e2b3c3aa065bb8e4462d9f8f9fe5289b66204541de8cbea5c8c123f3eef65
;
; The region preserves the RFC's three-space left margin, the deeper
; indentation of its two trailing ";" comment lines, and its internal
; blank line. Byte-exactness was confirmed by diffing the extracted
; region against the source lines, not by reading.
;
; The BEGIN/END markers are written as ABNF comments so that this file
; remains machine-checkable as ABNF (RFC 5234).
;
; NOT SELF-CONTAINED. These two rules reference "c-sexp" (Section 7.2,
; canonical.abnf) and "whitespace", "base-64-chars" and "base-64-end"
; (Section 7.1, advanced-transport.abnf). An ABNF tool fed this file
; alone reports four undefined rules. This is the RFC's own structure
; and nothing has been added here to close it.
;
; Start symbol: b-sexp.
; =====================================================================

; ---- BEGIN VERBATIM ----
   b-sexp         =  c-sexp / b-base-64

   b-base-64      =  "{" *whitespace *base-64-chars base-64-end "}"
                       ; encodes a c-sexp, which has a minimum
                       ; length of 2
; ---- END VERBATIM ----
